{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Complex.Circle","lean:module:Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.Bochner.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Measure.Lebesgue.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.ExpDecay","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.ImproperIntegrals","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":20,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral.integrableOn_kernel_Ioi_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral.integrableOn_kernel_Ioi_zero","kind":"theorem","line":689,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral.lean#L689-L701","doc":"**Full integrability on `(0, ∞)` (unconditional theorem).**  Near-`0` is\n`integrableOn_kernel_Ioc_zero_one`; the tail is `integrableOn_kernel_Ioi_one`.\nBoth are hypothesis-free, so the Faddeev kernel is integrable on all of\n`(0, ∞)` for every `b > 0` with no remaining analytic input — the def↔contour\nidentification (the `8e-29` pin) is the only open piece, and is assumed\nnowhere. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral.integrableOn_kernel_Ioc_zero_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral.integrableOn_kernel_Ioc_zero_one","kind":"theorem","line":655,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral.lean#L655-L686","doc":"**Near-`0` integrability (THEOREM, no hypotheses).**  The kernel is\nbounded on `(0, 1]` — the `−2z/t²` subtraction cancels the pole — hence\nintegrable there (`Ioc 0 1` has finite measure). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral.integrableOn_kernel_Ioi_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral.integrableOn_kernel_Ioi_one","kind":"theorem","line":242,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral.lean#L242-L333","doc":"**Tail integrability (unconditional theorem).**  The Faddeev kernel is\nintegrable on `[1, ∞)` for every `b > 0`: the oscillatory piece is dominated by\n`C·e^{−bt}` (`majorant_exp`), the subtraction by `2|z|·t^{−2}` (`majorant_inv`).\nAll kernel-specific analysis is proved here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral.phiB_mul_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral.phiB_mul_conj","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral.lean#L166-L177","doc":"**σ-unitarity** `Φ_b(z) · conj(Φ_b(z)) = 1` — the ring-involution form of\n`|Φ_b| = 1`, instantiating the σ-unitarity hypothesis of\n`prop:phi-b-unitary-bar-odd` at σ = complex conjugation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral.norm_fibreQParam","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral.norm_fibreQParam","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral.lean#L158-L164","doc":"**`|q_b| = 1` at every real `b`** — the fibre branch is exactly the\n`|q| = 1` regime (contrast `Im b² > 0`, where `|q_b| < 1` and the\nmodular-double product converges). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral.fibreQParam","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral.fibreQParam","kind":"def","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral.lean#L154-L156","doc":"The fibre modular parameter `q_b = e^{iπb²}` at real `b`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral.phiB_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral.phiB_zero","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral.lean#L132-L140","doc":"**Zero-argument value** `Φ_b(0) = exp(i·π(b²+b⁻²)/24)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral.phiB_inversion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral.phiB_inversion","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral.lean#L120-L130","doc":"**Inversion relation** `Φ_b(z)·Φ_b(−z) = exp(i(πz² + π(b²+b⁻²)/12))` —\nthe odd `J` cancels between the two factors. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral.norm_phiB","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral.norm_phiB","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral.lean#L115-L118","doc":"**Unitarity** `‖Φ_b(z)‖ = 1` — the phase is real. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral.J_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral.J_zero","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral.lean#L107-L113","doc":"`J(b, 0) = 0` (the integrand vanishes identically at `z = 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral.J_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral.J_odd","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral.lean#L100-L105","doc":"`J` is odd in `z` (no integrability needed: `∫ −f = −∫ f` is unconditional). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral.kernel_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral.kernel_odd","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral.lean#L94-L98","doc":"The kernel is odd in `z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral.phiB_self_dual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral.phiB_self_dual","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral.lean#L89-L92","doc":"**Modular-double self-duality** `Φ_{b⁻¹} = Φ_b` — sorry-free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral.phase_self_dual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral.phase_self_dual","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral.lean#L83-L87","doc":"The phase is self-dual: kernel symmetry plus `(b⁻¹)⁻¹ = b`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral.J_self_dual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral.J_self_dual","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral.lean#L76-L81","doc":"`J` is self-dual: `J(b⁻¹, z) = J(b, z)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral.kernel_self_dual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral.kernel_self_dual","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral.lean#L68-L74","doc":"The kernel is manifestly self-dual under `b ↔ b⁻¹` (the two `sinh` factors\nswap; the identities used are total, so `b = 0` needs no case split). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral.phiB","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral.phiB","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral.lean#L64-L66","doc":"The Faddeev `Φ_b` on the fibre saddle: a **defined** object (no axiom). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral.phase","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral.phase","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral.lean#L60-L62","doc":"The real Faddeev phase `−J/2 + πz²/2 + π(b²+b⁻²)/24`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral.J","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral.J","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral.lean#L57-L58","doc":"`J(b,z) = ∫₀^∞ kernel` — the real Faddeev phase integral. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral.kernel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral.kernel","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/FaddeevPhiBRealIntegral.lean#L51-L55","doc":"The real Faddeev kernel `sin(2zt)/(t·sinh(bt)·sinh(t/b)) − 2z/t²` (the\n`−2z/t²` subtraction cancels the `t→0` pole; totality of division makes the\ndefinition unconditional). ","signatureChunk":0}]}